<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Cenbank sets new weaker reais trade level.</title>
<headline>Brazil Cenbank sets new weaker reais trade level.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank set a new weaker trading level for the reais currency by buying dollars at 1.0525 reais and selling dollars at 1.0575 reais in a buy/sell tender in the commercial foreign exchange market, dealers said.</p>
<p>Under the previous mini-band set on Feb 28, the reais were traded between 1.0510 and 1.0560 reais to the dollar.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 2485415))</p>
